WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.480
As you can see, there is quite a bit of damage.

00:02.480 --> 00:05.880
As you can see here, granules have filled up your gutters.

00:05.880 --> 00:09.280
These granules are supposed to be what's protecting your home.

00:09.280 --> 00:11.480
When wind and hail hits your roof,

00:11.480 --> 00:13.040
it knocks out these granules,

00:13.040 --> 00:15.540
which reduces the lifespan of your roof.

00:15.540 --> 00:18.320
This is very similar to damage to the rest of the approvals

00:18.320 --> 00:19.860
we've gotten in the area.

00:19.860 --> 00:21.000
With that being said,

00:21.000 --> 00:23.180
insurance companies are always looking for ways

00:23.180 --> 00:24.800
to mitigate their losses.

00:24.800 --> 00:27.640
It's unfortunate, but that's how they make money.

00:27.640 --> 00:29.540
The most important part of this process

00:29.580 --> 00:31.580
is that when your insurance company comes out

00:31.580 --> 00:33.220
to run their inspection,

00:33.220 --> 00:34.960
we are here as storm experts

00:34.960 --> 00:38.520
to make sure you as a homeowner get a fair shake.

00:38.520 --> 00:40.080
If they are missing anything,

00:40.080 --> 00:42.900
we make sure they see all the damage that I just showed you.

00:42.900 --> 00:45.360
What I'm going to do now is run to my car,

00:45.360 --> 00:47.980
grab my iPad, and we can get this process started.

